            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a great frosting for my gingerbread men. I did find, however, that 1/4 cup of milk was far to much and produced a very runny frosting-more like a glaze. I kept adding sugar until it was more of a spreading consistancy. I also made a batch that was very stiff and put it into a bag and piped it onto the arms and legs-it was adorable!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GreenTongs5111"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I loved the frosting. I only used a tiny bit of milk and mixed it in slowly. Thanks leaving out the corn syrup. I added natural food coloring and my cookies turned out super cute!",
            "datePublished": "2023-12-25T00:27:23.647Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "FriskyTofu3516"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Super easy. I only added just enough milk(by the spoonful) to bring it together without lumps. Like toothpaste consistency (very thick). If it was too runny, I added a bit more sugar. I also added a bit of vanilla extract to it. I was surprised at how professional it tasted! Delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2024-12-12T06:16:44.974Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Ok, so I see a lot of the same stuff; \"IT'S TOO RUNNY\" or \"I HAD TO ADD FIVE CUPS OF SUGAR TO THICKEN IT\" and \"IT WOULDN'T THICKEN\". Please, please, please just read the directions, and carefully. Don't add all the milk. Do it teaspoon by teaspoon or tablespoon by tablespoon. You're eventually going to find your perfect thickness. If it's still too runny, try the refrigerator, and if you really need yo, add a bit of extra sugar, but not the whole bag. Also, add a bit of flavor if you feel like it. :)",
            "datePublished": "2021-12-22T03:12:35.337Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great on gingerbread! As others have said, more of a glaze than a frosting. I used about 1/6 milk with 1 cup sugar and the consistency was perfect. I added 1 drop red food coloring for a nice pink color and used them on my Valentine's day cookies. They were a big hit. Will use again. Thanks Alison!",
            "datePublished": "2006-02-19T17:34:38.920Z"
          },
          {
